Advanced Identity and Access Management (IAM) in DevSecOps
Learning Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the fundamentals of Identity and Access Management (IAM) in cloud environments • Identify and exploit privilege escalation vulnerabilities in AWS IAM trust policies • Implement Policy-as-Code using Open Policy Agent (OPA) for Kubernetes security • Configure least-privilege ServiceAccount bindings in Kubernetes • Apply security best practices for IAM in DevSecOps pipelines • Recognize common IAM misconfigurations and their security implications

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of cloud computing concepts • Familiarity with Linux command line operations • Basic knowledge of AWS services and concepts • Understanding of Kubernetes fundamentals • Basic knowledge of YAML file structure • Familiarity with JSON format

